#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# wavelet_matrix_plot

#% text
# `wavelet_matrix_plot(d)` shows the coefficients of discrete wavelet data of a matrix: for the discrete transform the arrays tiled as the transform stores them, the approximation in the corner and the details of each level around it; `wavelet_matrix_plot(d, r)` up to level r, `wavelet_matrix_plot(d, sel, f)` the values f(c) of the selected arrays.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For packet and stationary data, and with `plot_layout: "Grid"`, the arrays are drawn one by one in a grid. Complex coefficients are drawn by their modulus.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
wavelet_matrix_plot(discrete_wavelet_transform(diamond_matrix(32), automatic, 3))
#% output
#= image("wavelet_matrix_plot.files/wavelet_matrix_plot-1.svgz")

#% cell
wavelet_matrix_plot(discrete_wavelet_transform(cross_matrix(5), automatic, 2), plot_layout: "Grid")
#% output
#= image("wavelet_matrix_plot.files/wavelet_matrix_plot-2.svgz")

